⍝ lib/field.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 17: fields: finite fields GF(p) and GF(pⁿ), number fields ℚ(α), algebraic numbers
⍝ Everything is computed here, on base-(i−1) digit strings; helpers end in _fd.  A polynomial over GF(p) (p a prime) is the list of its
⍝ coefficients, lowest degree first, each a natural number in [0, p), without trailing zeros; the zero polynomial is [].  The field
⍝ GF(pⁿ) is the pair (p, m) of the prime and a monic irreducible polynomial m of degree n over GF(p): its elements are the polynomials
⍝ of degree < n.  The number field ℚ(α), α a root of an irreducible f ∈ ℚ[x], is ℚ[x]/(f) of lib/ring.imo.
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 1. polynomials over GF(p)
⍝ ---- the primitives, on polynomials already reduced modulo p: residues by the digit-level remainder of lib/poly.imo, sums of products
⍝ carried unreduced and reduced once, the division by a monic polynomial with only the leading entry reduced at each step
md_fd ∶ ℤ → ℕ → ℕ
md_fd ξ η ≔ (⊗ (rd_pl (↓ᶻ η) (↓ᶻ ξ)) (◀ 1))
ng_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
ng_fd π f ≔ (tr_fd (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd (⊖ κ) π)) f))
ad_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
ad_fd π f g ≔ (tr_fd (zl_fd (a b ↦ (md_fd (⊞ a b) π)) f g))
sb_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
sb_fd π f g ≔ (ad_fd π f (ng_fd π g))
sc_fd ∶ ℕ → ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
sc_fd π c f ≔ (tr_fd (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd (⊠ c κ) π)) f))
mu_fd ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
mu_fd ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (zl_fd ⊞ (⫶ (⊠ θ) η) (∷ 0 (mu_fd ι η)))) ⊥)
ml_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
ml_fd π f g ≔ (tr_fd (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd κ π)) (mu_fd f g)))
mo_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
mo_fd π f ≔ ((∅ f) ⊥ (sc_fd π (modinv (last f) π) f))
dr_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
dr_fd π f ≔ (tr_fd (⌄ (⫴ (a c ↦ (md_fd (⊠ a c) π)) (⍳ (ℓ f)) f)))
⍝ rest − c·τ (τ shorter than rest or as long); one step of the division by a monic polynomial with tail τ (highest entry first)
sbq_fd ∶ ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ
sbq_fd c τ rest ≔ (τ (t ts ↦ (rest (r rs ↦ (∷ (⊟ r (⊠ c t)) (sbq_fd c ts rs))) ⊥)) rest)
dl_fd ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔏 ℤ)
dl_fd π k τ ξ qs ≔ ((≐ k 0) (⊗ qs ξ) ((c ↦ (dl_fd π (⊟ k 1) τ (sbq_fd c τ (⌄ ξ)) (∷ c qs))) (md_fd (hd ξ) π)))
⍝ (quotient, remainder) of reduced f by reduced g ≠ 0
dv_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔏 ℕ)
dv_fd π f g ≔ ((≺ (fpdegree f) (fpdegree g)) (⊗ ⊥ f) ((iv ↦ ((τ ↦ ((r ↦ (⊗ (tr_fd (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd (⊠ iv κ) π)) (◀ r))) (tr_fd (reverse (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd κ π)) (▶ r)))))) (dl_fd π (⊞ (⊟ (fpdegree f) (fpdegree g)) 1) τ (reverse f) ⊥))) (⌄ (reverse (sc_fd π iv g))))) (modinv (last g) π)))
rm_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
rm_fd π f g ≔ (▶ (dv_fd π f g))
qo_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
qo_fd π f g ≔ (◀ (dv_fd π f g))
zl_fd ∶ (α → α → α) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
zl_fd φ ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∷ (φ θ θ′) (zl_fd φ ι ι′))) ξ)) η)
tr_fd ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
tr_fd ξ ≔ (foldr (θ ι ↦ ((∧ (∅ ι) (≐ θ 0)) ⊥ (∷ θ ι))) ⊥ ξ)
fpoly ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ fpoly(p, f): the coefficients reduced modulo p, trailing zeros removed — the canonical form over GF(p)
fpoly ξ η ≔ (tr_fd (⫶ (κ ↦ (md_fd κ ξ)) η))
fpadd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ f + g over GF(p)
fpadd ξ η ζ ≔ (ad_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ))
fpneg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ −f over GF(p)
fpneg ξ η ≔ (ng_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η))
fpsub ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ f − g over GF(p)
fpsub ξ η ζ ≔ (sb_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ))
fpscale ∶ ℕ → ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ c·f over GF(p)
fpscale ξ η ζ ≔ (sc_fd ξ η (fpoly ξ ζ))
fpmul ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ f · g over GF(p)
fpmul ξ η ζ ≔ (ml_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ))
fpdegree ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℤ      ⍝ the degree of a polynomial in canonical form (−1 for the zero polynomial)
fpdegree ξ ≔ (⊟ (ℓ ξ) 1)
fpmonic ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the monic multiple of f over GF(p) (the zero polynomial stays)
fpmonic ξ η ≔ (mo_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η))
⍝ division with remainder of canonical polynomials: (quotient, remainder), g ≠ 0
fpdivmod ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ fpdivmod(p, f, g): (quotient, remainder) with f = q·g + r, deg r < deg g; (0, f) for g = 0
fpdivmod ξ η ζ ≔ ((f g ↦ ((∅ g) (⊗ ⊥ f) (dv_fd ξ f g))) (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ))
fpquo ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the quotient of f by g over GF(p)
fpquo ξ η ζ ≔ (◀ (fpdivmod ξ η ζ))
fprem ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the remainder of f modulo g over GF(p)
fprem ξ η ζ ≔ (▶ (fpdivmod ξ η ζ))
gc_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
gc_fd π f g ≔ ((∅ g) (mo_fd π f) (gc_fd π g (▶ (dv_fd π f g))))
fpgcd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the monic gcd over GF(p) (gcd(0, 0) = 0)
fpgcd ξ η ζ ≔ (gc_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ))
⍝ extended Euclid: (g, (s, t)) with s·f + t·h = g monic
eg_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔏 ℕ))
eg_fd π r₀ r₁ s₀ s₁ t₀ t₁ ≔ ((∅ r₁) ((∅ r₀) (⊗ ⊥ (⊗ ⊥ ⊥)) ((λ′ ↦ (⊗ (sc_fd π λ′ r₀) (⊗ (sc_fd π λ′ s₀) (sc_fd π λ′ t₀)))) (modinv (last r₀) π))) ((qr ↦ (eg_fd π r₁ (▶ qr) s₁ (sb_fd π s₀ (ml_fd π (◀ qr) s₁)) t₁ (sb_fd π t₀ (ml_fd π (◀ qr) t₁)))) (dv_fd π r₀ r₁)))
fpegcd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) (𝔏 ℕ))      ⍝ fpegcd(p, f, g): (d, (s, t)) with s·f + t·g = d = gcd(f, g) monic
fpegcd ξ η ζ ≔ (eg_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η) (fpoly ξ ζ) (∷ 1 ⊥) ⊥ ⊥ (∷ 1 ⊥))
pw_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
pw_fd π f n m ≔ ((≐ n 0) (rm_fd π (∷ 1 ⊥) m) ((h ↦ (rm_fd π ((≐ (mod n 1100) 0) (ml_fd π h h) (ml_fd π f (ml_fd π h h))) m)) (pw_fd π f (div n 1100) m)))
fppowmod ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ fppowmod(p, f, n, m): fⁿ mod m over GF(p) by squaring (m = 0: fⁿ itself is not computed — the result is [])
fppowmod ξ η ζ ο ≔ ((m ↦ ((∅ m) ⊥ (pw_fd ξ (fprem ξ (fpoly ξ η) m) ζ m))) (fpoly ξ ο))
fpderiv ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the derivative f′ over GF(p)
fpderiv ξ η ≔ (dr_fd ξ (fpoly ξ η))
fpeval ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ f(a) over GF(p)
fpeval ξ η ζ ≔ (foldr (c acc ↦ (md_fd (⊞ c (⊠ ζ acc)) ξ)) 0 (fpoly ξ η))
fproots ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the roots of f in GF(p), ascending (every element for f = 0)
fproots ξ η ≔ (filter (a ↦ (≐ (fpeval ξ η a) 0)) (⍳ ξ))
⍝ irreducibility (Ben-Or): f of degree n ≥ 1 is irreducible iff gcd(x^(pᵏ) − x, f) = 1 for k = 1 … ⌊n/2⌋
bo_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔹
bo_fd π f k h ν ≔ ((≻ k ν) ⊤ ((hh ↦ ((≐ (fpdegree (gc_fd π f (sb_fd π hh (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥))))) 0) (bo_fd π f (⊞ k 1) hh ν) ⊥)) (pw_fd π h π f)))
fpirreducible ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ is f irreducible over GF(p)? (degree ≥ 1; Ben-Or's test)
fpirreducible ξ η ≔ ((f ↦ ((≺ (fpdegree f) 1) ⊥ (bo_fd ξ f 1 (fprem ξ (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)) f) (div (fpdegree f) 1100)))) (fpoly ξ η))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 2. factorisation over GF(p): square-free decomposition, distinct-degree factorisation, equal-degree splitting
⍝ the p-th root of a polynomial in x^p: the coefficients at the multiples of p
rt_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
rt_fd π c ≔ (c (θ ι ↦ (∷ θ (rt_fd π (drop (⊟ π 1) ι)))) ⊥)
⍝ Yun's algorithm in characteristic p: sf_fd π w c i = (the list of (zᵢ, i), the rest of c)
sf_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ)) (𝔏 ℕ)
sf_fd π w c i ≔ ((≺ (fpdegree w) 1) (⊗ ⊥ c) ((y ↦ ((z ↦ ((τ ↦ (⊗ ((≺ (fpdegree z) 1) (◀ τ) (∷ (⊗ z i) (◀ τ))) (▶ τ))) (sf_fd π y (qo_fd π c y) (⊞ i 1)))) (qo_fd π w y))) (gc_fd π w c)))
sq_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ)
sq_fd π f e ≔ ((c ↦ ((τ ↦ (⧺ (⫶ (zi ↦ (⊗ (◀ zi) (⊠ (▶ zi) e))) (◀ τ)) ((≺ (fpdegree (▶ τ)) 1) ⊥ (sq_fd π (rt_fd π (▶ τ)) (⊠ e π))))) (sf_fd π (qo_fd π f c) c 1))) (gc_fd π f (dr_fd π f)))
⍝ distinct-degree factorisation of a monic square-free g: pairs (product of the irreducible factors of degree d, d)
dd_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ)
dd_fd π g d xp ≔ ((≺ (fpdegree g) (⊠ 1100 d)) ((≺ (fpdegree g) 1) ⊥ (∷ (⊗ g (fpdegree g)) ⊥)) ((xq ↦ ((h ↦ ((≺ (fpdegree h) 1) (dd_fd π g (⊞ d 1) xq) ((g′ ↦ (∷ (⊗ h d) (dd_fd π g′ (⊞ d 1) (rm_fd π xq g′)))) (qo_fd π g h)))) (gc_fd π g (sb_fd π xq (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)))))) (pw_fd π xp π g)))
⍝ equal-degree splitting.  The candidates a: for odd p all monic polynomials of degree 1 … n − 1 (the first that splits is used), for
⍝ p = 2 the powers x^j.  A split: a proper factor of h.
mnc_fd ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
mnc_fd π j ≔ ((≐ j 0) (∷ (∷ 1 ⊥) ⊥) (concat (⫶ (c ↦ (⫶ (t ↦ (∷ c t)) (mnc_fd π (⊟ j 1)))) (⍳ π))))
cnd_fd ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
cnd_fd π n ≔ ((≐ π 1100) (⫶ (j ↦ (⧺ (replicate j 0) (∷ 1 ⊥))) (upto 1 (⊟ n 1))) (concat (⫶ (j ↦ (mnc_fd π j)) (upto 1 (⊟ n 1)))))
tr2_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
tr2_fd π a h d ≔ (rm_fd π (tr3_fd π a h d a) h)
tr3_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
tr3_fd π a h d s ≔ ((≐ d 1) s (tr3_fd π (pw_fd π a 1100 h) h (⊟ d 1) (ad_fd π s (pw_fd π a 1100 h))))
sp_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
sp_fd π h d a ≔ ((ν ↦ ((pr ↦ ((g ↦ ((pr g) g ((g′ ↦ ((pr g′) g′ ⊥)) (gc_fd π h ((≐ π 1100) (tr2_fd π a h d) (sb_fd π (pw_fd π a (div (⊟ (^ π d) 1) 1100) h) (∷ 1 ⊥))))))) (gc_fd π h a))) (g ↦ (∧ (≺ 0 (fpdegree g)) (≺ (fpdegree g) ν))))) (fpdegree h))
ed_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
ed_fd π h d ≔ ((≐ (fpdegree h) d) (∷ h ⊥) ((g ↦ (⧺ (ed_fd π g d) (ed_fd π (qo_fd π h g) d))) (hd (filter (g ↦ (¬ (∅ g))) (⫶ (sp_fd π h d) (cnd_fd π (fpdegree h)))))))
⍝ the whole factorisation of a monic polynomial: pairs (monic irreducible, multiplicity)
fa_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ)
fa_fd π f ≔ (concat (⫶ (zi ↦ (⫶ (g ↦ (⊗ g (▶ zi))) (concat (⫶ (hd′ ↦ (ed_fd π (◀ hd′) (▶ hd′))) (dd_fd π (◀ zi) 1 (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥))))))) (sq_fd π f 1)))
⍝ sort the pairs by (degree, then the coefficients from the highest degree down)
cm_fd ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔒
cm_fd ξ η ≔ ((⋚ (ℓ ξ) (ℓ η)) ⋖ (cl_fd (reverse ξ) (reverse η)) ⋗)
cl_fd ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔒
cl_fd ξ η ≔ (ξ (a as ↦ (η (b bs ↦ ((⋚ a b) ⋖ (cl_fd as bs) ⋗)) ≖)) ≖)
in_fd ∶ 𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ)
in_fd θ ξ ≔ (ξ (h t ↦ ((cm_fd (◀ θ) (◀ h)) (∷ θ ξ) (∷ θ ξ) (∷ h (in_fd θ t)))) (∷ θ ⊥))
fpfactor ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 (𝔓 (𝔏 ℕ) ℕ))      ⍝ fpfactor(p, f): the complete factorisation over GF(p): (c, [(g, k)]) with f = c·Π gᵏ, c the leading coefficient, every g monic and irreducible, sorted by degree then coefficients; (0, []) for f = 0, (c, []) for a constant
fpfactor ξ η ≔ ((f ↦ ((∅ f) (⊗ 0 ⊥) (⊗ (last f) (foldr in_fd ⊥ (fa_fd ξ (fpmonic ξ f)))))) (fpoly ξ η))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 3. irreducible and primitive polynomials, counting
numirreducible ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the number of monic irreducible polynomials of degree n over GF(p): (1/n)·Σ_(d | n) μ(d) p^(n/d)
numirreducible ξ η ≔ ((≐ η 0) 0 (div (sumof (⫶ (d ↦ (⊠ (mobius d) (^ ξ (div η d)))) (divisors η))) η))
cf_fd ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
cf_fd π n k ≔ (⫶ (j ↦ (mod (div k (^ π j)) π)) (⍳ n))
mp_fd ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
mp_fd π n k ≔ (⧺ (cf_fd π n k) (∷ 1 ⊥))
irreduciblepoly ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ irreduciblepoly(p, n): the first monic irreducible polynomial of degree n ≥ 1 over GF(p), the candidates xⁿ + Σ aⱼxʲ taken in the order of Σ aⱼpʲ (x² + x + 1 over GF(2), x³ + x + 1, x⁴ + x + 1, …)
irreduciblepoly ξ η ≔ (hd (filter (f ↦ (fpirreducible ξ f)) (⫶ (k ↦ (mp_fd ξ η k)) (iterate (k ↦ (⊞ k 1)) 0))))
⍝ the order of x modulo f is p^n − 1: x^((p^n − 1)/r) ≠ 1 for every prime r dividing p^n − 1
pr_fd ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔹
pr_fd π f n ≔ ((q ↦ (∧ (eqlist ≐ (pw_fd π (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)) q f) (∷ 1 ⊥)) (∀ₗ (r ↦ (¬ (eqlist ≐ (pw_fd π (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)) (div q (◀ r)) f) (∷ 1 ⊥)))) (factor q)))) (⊟ (^ π n) 1))
isprimitivepoly ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ is f a primitive polynomial over GF(p) — monic, irreducible, and x generates the multiplicative group of GF(p)[x]/(f)?
isprimitivepoly ξ η ≔ ((f ↦ (∧ (¬ (∅ f)) (∧ (≐ (last f) 1) (∧ (fpirreducible ξ f) (pr_fd ξ f (fpdegree f)))))) (fpoly ξ η))
primitivepoly ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ primitivepoly(p, n): the first monic primitive polynomial of degree n ≥ 1 over GF(p), in the order of irreduciblepoly (x² + x + 1 and x³ + x + 1 over GF(2); for n = 1 the first x + a whose root −a is a primitive root modulo p)
primitivepoly ξ η ≔ (hd (filter (f ↦ (∧ (fpirreducible ξ f) (pr_fd ξ f η))) (⫶ (k ↦ (mp_fd ξ η k)) (iterate (k ↦ (⊞ k 1)) 0))))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 4. the finite field GF(pⁿ) = (p, m): the elements are the polynomials over GF(p) of degree < n, arithmetic modulo the irreducible m
gf ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ gf(p, n): the field GF(pⁿ) as the pair (p, m), m = primitivepoly(p, n) (so that x is a generator of the multiplicative group); another irreducible modulus m can be used as the pair (p, m)
gf ξ η ≔ (⊗ ξ (primitivepoly ξ η))
gfchar ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the characteristic p of the field
gfchar ξ ≔ (◀ ξ)
gfmodulus ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the defining polynomial m of the field
gfmodulus ξ ≔ (▶ ξ)
gfdegree ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the degree n of the field over GF(p)
gfdegree ξ ≔ (fpdegree (▶ ξ))
gfsize ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ      ⍝ the number of elements pⁿ
gfsize ξ ≔ (^ (◀ ξ) (fpdegree (▶ ξ)))
gfelement ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the element of the field represented by a polynomial over GF(p) (reduced modulo p and m)
gfelement ξ η ≔ (fprem (◀ ξ) (fpoly (◀ ξ) η) (▶ ξ))
gfadd ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ a + b in GF(pⁿ)
gfadd ξ η ζ ≔ (fprem (◀ ξ) (fpadd (◀ ξ) η ζ) (▶ ξ))
gfsub ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ a − b in GF(pⁿ)
gfsub ξ η ζ ≔ (fprem (◀ ξ) (fpsub (◀ ξ) η ζ) (▶ ξ))
gfneg ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ −a in GF(pⁿ)
gfneg ξ η ≔ (fprem (◀ ξ) (fpneg (◀ ξ) η) (▶ ξ))
gfmul ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ a · b in GF(pⁿ)
gfmul ξ η ζ ≔ (fprem (◀ ξ) (fpmul (◀ ξ) η ζ) (▶ ξ))
gfinv ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the inverse of a in GF(pⁿ) (extended Euclid with the modulus); [] for a = 0
gfinv ξ η ≔ ((σ ↦ ((eqlist ≐ (◀ σ) (∷ 1 ⊥)) (fprem (◀ ξ) (◀ (▶ σ)) (▶ ξ)) ⊥)) (fpegcd (◀ ξ) (gfelement ξ η) (▶ ξ)))
gfdiv ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ a / b in GF(pⁿ) ([] for b = 0)
gfdiv ξ η ζ ≔ (gfmul ξ η (gfinv ξ ζ))
gfpow ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ aᵉ in GF(pⁿ) by squaring (e < 0: a power of the inverse; 0⁰ = 1)
gfpow ξ η ζ ≔ ((≺ ζ 0) (pw_fd (◀ ξ) (gfinv ξ η) (⊖ ζ) (▶ ξ)) (pw_fd (◀ ξ) (gfelement ξ η) ζ (▶ ξ)))
gfelements ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ all pⁿ elements, in the order of Σ aⱼpʲ (0 = [] first)
gfelements ξ ≔ (⫶ (k ↦ (tr_fd (cf_fd (◀ ξ) (fpdegree (▶ ξ)) k))) (⍳ (gfsize ξ)))
⍝ multiplicative order: from q − 1 down, removing each prime r while a^(o/r) = 1
ro_fd ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → ℕ → ℕ
ro_fd F a o r ≔ ((∧ (≐ (mod o r) 0) (eqlist ≐ (gfpow F a (div o r)) (∷ 1 ⊥))) (ro_fd F a (div o r) r) o)
gforder ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ the multiplicative order of a in GF(pⁿ) (0 for a = 0)
gforder ξ η ≔ ((a ↦ ((∅ a) 0 (foldl (o r ↦ (ro_fd ξ a o (◀ r))) (⊟ (gfsize ξ) 1) (factor (⊟ (gfsize ξ) 1))))) (gfelement ξ η))
gfisprimitive ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ does a generate the multiplicative group of GF(pⁿ)?
gfisprimitive ξ η ≔ (≐ (gforder ξ η) (⊟ (gfsize ξ) 1))
gfprimitive ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the first primitive element of GF(pⁿ) in the order of gfelements
gfprimitive ξ ≔ (hd (filter (a ↦ (gfisprimitive ξ a)) (gfelements ξ)))
lg_fd ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → ℤ
lg_fd F g a k cur ≔ ((eqlist ≐ cur a) k ((⩾ k (gfsize F)) 11101 (lg_fd F g a (⊞ k 1) (gfmul F cur g))))
gflog ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ → ℤ      ⍝ gflog(F, g, a): the least k ≥ 0 with gᵏ = a (the discrete logarithm by repeated multiplication), −1 if there is none
gflog ξ η ζ ≔ (lg_fd ξ (gfelement ξ η) (gfelement ξ ζ) 0 (∷ 1 ⊥))
gffrob ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the Frobenius map a ↦ aᵖ
gffrob ξ η ≔ (gfpow ξ η (◀ ξ))
⍝ the conjugates a, aᵖ, aᵖ², … (n of them, with repetitions)
cj_fd ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
cj_fd F k a ≔ ((≐ k 0) ⊥ (∷ a (cj_fd F (⊟ k 1) (gffrob F a))))
gftrace ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ Tr(a) = a + aᵖ + … + aᵖ^(n−1), an element of GF(p)
gftrace ξ η ≔ ((s ↦ ((∅ s) 0 (hd s))) (foldl (u v ↦ (gfadd ξ u v)) ⊥ (cj_fd ξ (gfdegree ξ) (gfelement ξ η))))
gfnorm ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ N(a) = a·aᵖ·…·aᵖ^(n−1) = a^((pⁿ − 1)/(p − 1)), an element of GF(p)
gfnorm ξ η ≔ ((s ↦ ((∅ s) 0 (hd s))) (foldl (u v ↦ (gfmul ξ u v)) (∷ 1 ⊥) (cj_fd ξ (gfdegree ξ) (gfelement ξ η))))
gfconjugates ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the distinct conjugates of a over GF(p): a, aᵖ, … until a repeats
gfconjugates ξ η ≔ ((a ↦ (take (gfdeg_fd ξ a) (cj_fd ξ (gfdegree ξ) a))) (gfelement ξ η))
gfdeg_fd ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ
gfdeg_fd F a ≔ (hd (filter (k ↦ (eqlist ≐ (gfpow F a (^ (◀ F) k)) a)) (upto 1 (gfdegree F))))
gfminpoly ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the minimal polynomial of a over GF(p) — monic, irreducible, of degree dividing n: Π (y − c) over the conjugates c of a
gfminpoly ξ η ≔ ((a ↦ (⫶ (e ↦ ((∅ e) 0 (hd e))) (foldl (P c ↦ (zl_fd (u v ↦ (gfsub ξ u v)) (∷ ⊥ P) (⫶ (e ↦ (gfmul ξ c e)) P))) (∷ (∷ 1 ⊥) ⊥) (gfconjugates ξ a)))) (gfelement ξ η))
gfsqrt ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ all square roots of a in GF(pⁿ): [] if a is a non-square, [0] for 0, two roots (±r) otherwise, one in characteristic 2
gfsqrt ξ η ≔ ((a ↦ (filter (e ↦ (eqlist ≐ (gfmul ξ e e) a)) (gfelements ξ))) (gfelement ξ η))
gfissquare ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ is a a square in GF(pⁿ)? (Euler's criterion a^((q−1)/2) = 1 for odd characteristic; every element in characteristic 2)
gfissquare ξ η ≔ ((a ↦ ((∨ (∅ a) (≐ (◀ ξ) 1100)) ⊤ (eqlist ≐ (gfpow ξ a (div (⊟ (gfsize ξ) 1) 1100)) (∷ 1 ⊥)))) (gfelement ξ η))
gfroots ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℤ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the roots in GF(pⁿ) of a polynomial whose coefficients are elements of the field (lowest degree first), in the order of gfelements
gfroots ξ η ≔ (filter (e ↦ (∅ (foldr (c acc ↦ (gfadd ξ c (gfmul ξ e acc))) ⊥ η))) (gfelements ξ))
gfsubfields ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the degrees of the subfields of GF(pⁿ) over GF(p): the divisors of n (one subfield of each such degree)
gfsubfields ξ ≔ (divisors ξ)
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 5. number fields ℚ(α) = ℚ[x]/(f), f irreducible over ℚ: the elements are the polynomials of degree < n = deg f (the arithmetic is qradd,
⍝ qrmul, qrinv, qrpow of lib/ring.imo).  The multiplication by a is a linear map; its matrix in the basis 1, α, …, αⁿ⁻¹ gives the
⍝ characteristic polynomial, minimal polynomial, norm and trace of a.
nfmatrix ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ nfmatrix(f, a): the matrix of the multiplication by a in ℚ[x]/(f) in the basis 1, x, …, xⁿ⁻¹ (column j: the coordinates of a·xʲ)
nfmatrix ξ η ≔ ((ν ↦ (transpose (⫶ (j ↦ ((c ↦ (⧺ c (replicate (⊟ ν (ℓ c)) 0))) (qrmul ξ η (⧺ (replicate j 0) (∷ 1 ⊥))))) (⍳ ν)))) (deg ξ))
nfcharpoly ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ      ⍝ the characteristic polynomial of a over ℚ (degree n; a power of the minimal polynomial)
nfcharpoly ξ η ≔ (charpoly (nfmatrix ξ η))
nfminpoly ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ      ⍝ the minimal polynomial of a over ℚ (monic; of degree dividing n)
nfminpoly ξ η ≔ (minpoly (nfmatrix ξ η))
nfdegree ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → ℕ      ⍝ the degree [ℚ(a) : ℚ] of the element a (the degree of its minimal polynomial)
nfdegree ξ η ≔ (deg (nfminpoly ξ η))
nftrace ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → ℚ      ⍝ the trace Tr(a) of a ∈ ℚ(α) over ℚ (the trace of the multiplication matrix: the sum of the conjugates of a)
nftrace ξ η ≔ (trace (nfmatrix ξ η))
nfnorm ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → ℚ      ⍝ the norm N(a) of a ∈ ℚ(α) over ℚ (the determinant of the multiplication matrix: the product of the conjugates of a)
nfnorm ξ η ≔ (det (nfmatrix ξ η))
nfisintegral ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔹      ⍝ is a an algebraic integer? (its minimal polynomial has integer coefficients)
nfisintegral ξ η ≔ (∀ₗ (c ↦ (≐ (denom c) 1)) (nfminpoly ξ η))
nfdiscriminant ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℚ      ⍝ the discriminant of the polynomial f — the discriminant of the basis 1, α, …, αⁿ⁻¹ of ℚ(α) (the field discriminant divides it)
nfdiscriminant ξ ≔ (discriminant ξ)
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 6. algebraic numbers: the minimal polynomials of α + β, α·β, −α, 1/α, αᵏ, α^(1/k) for α, β roots of f, g.  Each function returns the
⍝ monic irreducible factors over ℚ of the polynomial Π (x − γ), γ running over the combinations of ALL roots of f and g — the minimal
⍝ polynomial of the combination of two given roots is one of them.  The polynomial is the resultant Res_y(f(y), G(x, y)), evaluated at
⍝ as many integers x as its degree plus one and interpolated.
fc_fd ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)
fc_fd ξ ≔ (⫶ (g ↦ (polymonic g)) (⫶ ◀ (▶ (polyfactor ξ))))
hp_fd ∶ (ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ) → ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ
hp_fd G ν f ≔ ((pts ↦ (interpolate pts (⫶ (t ↦ (resultant f (G t))) pts))) (⍳ (⊞ ν 1)))
algsum ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algsum(f, g): the irreducible factors of the polynomial with the roots α + β (α a root of f, β of g); f, g non-constant
algsum ξ η ≔ (fc_fd (hp_fd (t ↦ (polycompose η (∷ t (∷ 11101 ⊥)))) (⊠ (deg ξ) (deg η)) ξ))
algneg ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algneg(f): the irreducible factors of the polynomial with the roots −α
algneg ξ ≔ (fc_fd (polycompose ξ (∷ 0 (∷ 11101 ⊥))))
algdiff ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algdiff(f, g): the polynomial with the roots α − β
algdiff ξ η ≔ (algsum ξ (polycompose η (∷ 0 (∷ 11101 ⊥))))
algprod ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algprod(f, g): the irreducible factors of the polynomial with the roots α·β; [x] when f or g has the root 0 (f(0) = 0 or g(0) = 0: take f, g without the factor x)
algprod ξ η ≔ ((∨ (≐ (hd ξ) 0) (≐ (hd η) 0)) (∷ (∷ 0 (∷ 1 ⊥)) ⊥) ((μ ↦ (fc_fd (hp_fd (t ↦ (⫶ (j ↦ (⊠ (nth η (⊟ μ j)) (^ t (⊟ μ j)))) (⍳ (⊞ μ 1)))) (⊠ (deg ξ) μ) ξ))) (deg η)))
alginv ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ alginv(f): the irreducible factors of the polynomial with the roots 1/α (the reversed polynomial; the root 0 is dropped)
alginv ξ ≔ (fc_fd (reverse ξ))
algquot ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algquot(f, g): the polynomial with the roots α/β
algquot ξ η ≔ (algprod ξ (reverse η))
algpow ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algpow(f, k): the polynomial with the roots αᵏ (k ≥ 1)
algpow ξ η ≔ (fc_fd (hp_fd (t ↦ (∷ t (⧺ (replicate (⊟ η 1) 0) (∷ 11101 ⊥)))) (deg ξ) ξ))
algroot ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)      ⍝ algroot(f, k): the irreducible factors of f(xᵏ), the polynomials with the roots α^(1/k) (k ≥ 1)
algroot ξ η ≔ (fc_fd (polycompose ξ (⧺ (replicate η 0) (∷ 1 ⊥))))
